          "The coordinates are dimensionless indices referring to entries in an internal lookup table; the agent must call a separate resolve_site_coordinates tool to obtain the actual spatial positions.": 0,
          "The coordinates are in Cartesian (\u00c5) units, not fractional; the z-values (~18.5 \u00c5) represent absolute heights within the cell, and the ontop sites have slightly higher z than hollow sites (~0.07 \u00c5 difference) because ontop sites sit directly above surface atoms while hollow sites sit between them.": 1
